<title>FINLAND: FINNISH STATE 1997 DEBT REPAYMENT SCHEDULE.</title>
<headline>FINNISH STATE 1997 DEBT REPAYMENT SCHEDULE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following schedule of</p>
<p>maturing Finnish state debt has been compiled by Reuters from</p>
<p>government sources:</p>
<p> Title and Interest Rate	 Date of maturity  Amount, mln FIM</p>
<p> 11.0% Loan of '92, II		 June 15	  12,631</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  June 16	  3,640</p>
<p> Floating Rate PSC Loan '93*	 July 7	   6</p>
<p> 8.0% Yen Loan '90		     July 11	611(JPY 15,000)</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  July 15	  1,750</p>
<p>Floating Rate</p>
<p> Dollar Loan '92			 July 17	  4,541 ($1,000)</p>
<p> 6.80% Loan of '95		     Aug 7	    1,286</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  Aug 15	   4,773</p>
<p> 8.0% Loan of '87, IV		  Aug 17	   106</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  Sept 15	  3,932</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  Oct 15	   4,552</p>
<p> 7-3/4% Loan of '87		    Oct 19	   83</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  Nov 14	   4,338</p>
<p> 7-3/4% Deutsche Mark Loan '92     Nov 20	3,013 (DEM 1,000)</p>
<p> 6-3/4% Dollar Loan '93		Nov 24	   9,081 ($2,000)</p>
<p> 6-3/4% Dollar Loan '93		Nov 24	   4,541 ($1,000)</p>
<p> 5.10%  Loan '95			 Dec 4	    1,684</p>
<p> Treasury bills			  Dec 15	   3,286</p>
<p>Note: Fluctuations in exchange rates will change the value</p>
<p>of foreign currency debt in markka.</p>
<p>The outstanding amount of Treasury bills by maturity at June</p>
<p>10, 1997. These will be updated after each weekly T-bills</p>
<p>auction.</p>
<p>(*Postipankki's currency basket, exchange rate was</p>
<p>calculated on Oct 31, 1996).</p>
<p>--Veera Heinonen, Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 240</p>
